/// A timeout `idle.after` was asked about, and whether the seat has been
/// idle that long.
record IdleTimeout key timeout {
  /// How long without input it waits for.
  timeout: duration
  /// The seat has had no input for at least `timeout`.
  idle: bool
}

/// Whether the user is away, from the compositor's idle notifications
/// (ext-idle-notify-v1). What inhibits idling (a video playing, a
/// surface's `inhibit_idle: true`) holds them back.
service idle {
  /// The compositor tells how long the user has been away
  /// (ext-idle-notify-v1); while false, `idle.after` is false.
  available: bool
  /// The timeouts `idle.after` was asked about, each with whether the
  /// seat has been idle that long, by timeout.
  timeouts: [IdleTimeout]
  /// True once the seat has had no input for `timeout`, false again at
  /// the next input: `panel Saver { open: idle.after(300s) }`.
  fn after(timeout: duration) -> bool
}
